    "created_at": "2026-05-12T08:29:40Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-05-12T09:02:17Z",
    "body": "\"fixed\" how? the browser is doing exactly what the author is asking for ... \"when the page is loaded, move/force focus directly to this thing here\". what do you think screen readers should do here?\n\nand to clarify, i think the original issue is slightly wrong here. it's comparing how a screen reader normally reacts when a page is loaded - i.e. in absence of any other user input, it just starts reading the page content sequentially by itself - versus focus already being set somewhere. it's not that the content is ignored/suppressed. it's just that once focus is explicitly moved somewhere, the SR doesn't do its automatic \"let me just read through the document\" behavior, and instead reads out/announces where the focus is, and then waits for further user input.\n\ntrying to somehow \"fix\" this is not possible - if focus IS on a control, having the screen reader then continue reading/announcing what comes before or after it is deceptive for the SR user.\n\nEDIT: apologies, my tone here was unnecessarily combative ... it's just that i too often see \"the SR should fix this\" as an \"answer\" to problems that have nothing to do with SRs themselves",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
