    "created_at": "2026-05-12T08:32:00Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-05-12T08:33:29Z",
    "body": "the actual fix/solution would be for browsers to implement an accessibility setting, so users can explicitly say to their browser \"ignore the `autofocus` attribute and do *not* set focus automatically to things, even if the page/author requested it\". (which then would actually make it a more accessible way to do things, compared to JavaScript focus hacks on page load, because it's imperative and can therefore be enforced at browser level easily)",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
